  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Scaler** `scalers/02-latency-p95.yaml` &nbsp;\u00b7&nbsp; **Load** `loadgen/latency.yaml` (10 connections \u00d7 `/delay/1`) &nbsp;\u00b7&nbsp; **Expect** p95 jumps far above the 100 ms target, so the pods run quickly to the maximum (10) and stay there.\n\np95 reads ~2.4 s, not 1 s: the histogram has 1 s and 2.5 s buckets and `histogram_quantile` interpolates inside the bucket. Adding pods cannot make a deliberately slow endpoint faster, so latency stays high. That is the trap of scaling on latency alone; see the notes in `scalers/02-latency-p95.yaml`."
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p50",
      "description": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{namespace=\"${namespace}\",job=\"${job}\",path!~\"readyz|healthz|metrics\"}[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "blue"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "id": 2,
